              <fr:month>2</fr:month>
              <fr:day>12</fr:day>
            </fr:date>
            <fr:uri>https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-001Z/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>sss-001Z</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/sss-001Z/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Unambiguity via the Diagonal Being an Isomorphism">Unambiguity via the Diagonal Being an Isomorphism</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p><fr:link href="/sss-001V/" title="Finite Unambiguity" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-001V/" display-uri="sss-001V" type="local">Finite unambiguity</fr:link> does not serve as an adequate definition of unambiguity that is equivalent to <fr:link href="/sss-001T/" title="Unambiguity as Subterminality" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-001T/" display-uri="sss-001T" type="local">[sss-001T]</fr:link> and <fr:link href="/sss-001U/" title="Unambiguity as Unique Map into Codomain" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-001U/" display-uri="sss-001U" type="local">[sss-001U]</fr:link>. However, the definition attempted via finite unambiguity can be refined to something that is equivalent to these.
</html:p>
            <html:p>
A grammar <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A]]></fr:tex> is unambiguous if <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Delta  : A \vdash  A \And  A]]></fr:tex> is an isomorphism. Equivalently, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A]]></fr:tex> is unambiguous if <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\pi _{1} : A \And  A \vdash  A]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\pi _{2} : A \And  A \vdash  A]]></fr:tex> are equal.
</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
      </fr:mainmatter>
